# central-app `/api/v1` routes

## Rule

Any route that should live under `/api/v1` in `central-app` **must** be registered with
`App\Modules\V1\Shared\Support\ApiV1::routes(...)`.

Do **not** write `Route::prefix('api/v1')` or duplicate the `api` middleware group by hand
(in a module `routes/api.php`, a service provider, or a test).

## Pattern

```php
use App\Modules\V1\Shared\Support\ApiV1;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;

// Module routes/api.php (preferred)
ApiV1::routes(function (): void {
    Route::post('auth/login', LoginController::class);
});

// Or pass a file path
ApiV1::routes(__DIR__.'/auth.php');
```

Load the module route file from that module’s `{Name}ServiceProvider` via
`$this->loadRoutesFrom(__DIR__.'/routes/api.php')` — keep prefix/middleware out of the provider.

## Anti-patterns

```php
// ❌ BAD — hand-rolled prefix
Route::prefix('api/v1')->middleware('api')->group(...);

// ❌ BAD — full path that bypasses ApiV1
Route::middleware('api')->post('/api/v1/auth/login', ...);

// ✅ GOOD
ApiV1::routes(fn () => Route::post('auth/login', ...));
```

## Applies to

- Module `routes/api.php` files under `central-app/app/Modules/V1/*`
- Tests that register temporary `/api/v1` endpoints
- Any future central JSON API domain (not Filament `web` routes)

Follow the skill `bltdreeg-central-api-v1-routes` when adding or moving API routes.
